<title>USA: Transkaryotic issues European patent.</title>
<headline>Transkaryotic issues European patent.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, MASS. 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transkaryotic Therapies Inc said a European patent was issued related to its non-viral gene therapy technology.</p>
<p>The technology, Transkaryotic Therapy, is a non-viral, ex vivo system based on the genetic modification of patients' cells, the company said.</p>
<p>The patent, issued to the General Hospital Corp, covers the use of cells genetically-modified by non-viral techniques in gene therapy and methods of producing such cells.</p>
<p>The company said it has reached no licensing agreements stemming from the patent to date, although it expects to seek agreements in the near future. It did not specify when.</p>
</text>
